  "name": "Chicken with Morels and a Sherry Sauce",
  "text": "Chicken with Morels and a Sherry Sauce\n\nPreparation time: 15 minutes\n\nIngredients\n\nFor the chicken\n\n7 g dried morel mushrooms,\n\n2 chicken breasts.\n\nSalt & pepper,\n\n1/2 tbsp unsalted butter,\n\n30 g button mushrooms,\n\n50 ml of dry white wine or sherry (boiled for 30 seconds to reduce the alcohol,\n\n100 ml double cream.\n\nFor the leeks\n\nSalt,\n\n1/2 tbsp unsalted butter,\n\n2 leeks (sliced into 2 cm pieces)\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Soak the morels in 125 ml of water (ideally overnight).\n\n2. Drain the morels, reserving the juice, sieve to remove any grit, squeezing the mushrooms dry. Rinse the mushrooms to remove any grit. Chop the roughly.\n\n3. Season the chicken breasts and Brown in butter over a medium heat for 3 minutes per side. Remove from the pan.\n\n4. Add the morel and button  mushrooms to the pan with a pinch of salt and soften for 2 minutes. Add the boiled wine or sherry and the mushroom juice and double cream. Bring to the boil and add the chicken breasts. Reduce the heat to a bare simmer and cook for 7 minutes.\n\n5. Remove the chicken breasts and keep warm. Increase the heat, and boil down the sauce until it coats the back of a spoon. Season.\n\n6. Boil the chopped leaks in 100ml of water with the butter and salt with the lid on for 3 minutes.\n\n7. Return the chicken breasts to the sauce, warm through, then serve over the leeks.",
  "prepTime": "PT15M",
  "cookTime": "PT30M",
  "recipeIngredient": [
    "For the chicken: 7 g dried morel mushrooms,",
    "For the chicken: 2 chicken breasts.",
    "For the chicken: Salt & pepper,",
    "For the chicken: 1/2 tbsp unsalted butter,",
    "For the chicken: 30 g button mushrooms,",
    "For the chicken: 50 ml of dry white wine or sherry (boiled for 30 seconds to reduce the alcohol,",
    "For the chicken: 100 ml double cream.",
    "For the leeks: Salt,",
